              "feedback": {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Incorrect. There are different algebraic approaches for solving for the concentration of the first metal at the point when the second metal ion begins to precipitate, but all approaches rely on identifying which metal ion precipitates first and on combining the equilibrium expressions for each metal bromide. First, identify which ion precipitates first, Ag"
                      },
                      {
                        "sup": true,
                        "text": "+ "
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "or Pb"
                      },
                      {
                        "sup": true,
                        "text": "2+"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ", by examining the "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "K"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "sp"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " values of the two metal bromide solids. Remember, the substance with the lowest "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "K"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "sp"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " value has the lowest equilibrium concentration of dissolved solute and lowest solubility and will precipitate before a substance with a higher "
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "text": "K"
                      },
                      {
                        "em": true,
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "sp"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " value. Next, consider the combined solubility equilibria at the point when the second ion begins to precipitate:"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "d64523e9f290492497ebb895bcc136ad",
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": ""
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          }
                        ],
                        "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                        "src": "\\text{Ag}^+(aq) + \\text{Pb}^{2+}(aq) + 3 \\, \\text{Br}^-(aq) \\rightleftharpoons \\text{AgBr}(s) + \\text{PbBr}_2(s)",
                        "subtype": "latex",
                        "type": "formula_inline"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "bf91adfe341849f1bf594647bff5bfda",
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "At this point, the concentration of the second ion is equal to the initial concentration of that ion in solution, which is given, because the ion is just beginning to precipitate. To solve for the unknown concentration of the first ion, consider the solubility equilibria for each metal bromide and their equilibrium expressions:"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "eee361d4e15a4cab8eb09a1abd6efd99",
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": ""
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          }
                        ],
                        "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                        "src": "\\text{AgBr}(s) \\rightleftharpoons \\text{Ag}^+(aq) + \\text{Br}^-(aq) \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ K_{sp1} = [\\text{Ag}^+][\\text{Br}^-]",
                        "subtype": "latex",
                        "type": "formula_inline"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "cc46b63ee96346e485fb57ce6bf09221",
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": ""
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          }
                        ],
                        "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                        "src": "\\text{PbBr}_2(s) \\rightleftharpoons \\text{Pb}^{2+}(aq) + 2\\text{Br}^-(aq) \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ K_{sp2} = [\\text{Pb}^{2+}][\\text{Br}^-]^2",
                        "subtype": "latex",
                        "type": "formula_inline"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "a8f8747ca94d45489c8cbb6da86f6e70",
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Use algebra to rearrange the equilibrium expression of the first ion to precipitate in terms of only "
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          }
                        ],
                        "legacyBlockRendered": false,
                        "src": "K_{sp1}",
                        "subtype": "latex",
                        "type": "formula_inline"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ", "
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          }
                        ],
                        "legacyBlockRendered": false,
                        "src": "K_{sp2}",
                        "subtype": "latex",
                        "type": "formula_inline"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ", and the second ion concentration. Be sure to substitute for the concentration of bromide "
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": ""
                          }
                        ],
                        "legacyBlockRendered": false,
                        "src": "\\text{Br}^-",
                        "subtype": "latex",
                        "type": "formula_inline"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " by using the other equilibrium expression for the second ion. "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "cf3465d551744b7c983cba218d65bcf7",
                    "type": "p"
                  },
