    "stem": {
      "content": [
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "A beaker contains @@conc@@ M silver and lead(II) ions. A concentrated sodium bromide solution is added dropwise and the solution is mixed thoroughly. "
            },
            {
              "em": true,
              "text": "K"
            },
            {
              "em": true,
              "sub": true,
              "text": "sp"
            },
            {
              "text": " for AgBr = 5.35×10"
            },
            {
              "sup": true,
              "text": "-13"
            },
            {
              "text": " and "
            },
            {
              "em": true,
              "text": "K"
            },
            {
              "em": true,
              "sub": true,
              "text": "sp"
            },
            {
              "text": " = PbBr"
            },
            {
              "sub": true,
              "text": "2"
            },
            {
              "text": " = 6.60×10"
            },
            {
              "sup": true,
              "text": "-6"
            },
            {
              "text": ", so the metal cations will precipitate sequentially. "
            }
          ],
          "id": "iu2db36i581xdzq",
          "type": "p"
        },
        {
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "At some point after the first metal ion begins to precipitate as a metal bromide solid, the second metal ion will begin to precipitate as a metal bromide solid. What is the concentration of the first metal ion at this point?"
            }
          ],
